{"xson":[{"/iati-activities/iati-activity":[{"/activity-date":[{"@iso-date":"2020-06-02","@type":"2"},{"@iso-date":"2028-07-31","@type":"3"}],"/activity-status@code":"2","/collaboration-type@code":"2","/contact-info":[{"/organisation/narrative":[{"1":"International Fund for Agricultural Development","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/person-name/narrative":[{"1":"Norvilus, Marcelin","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/telephone":[{"1":"+390654591"}],"/website":[{"1":"http://www.ifad.org"}],"@type":"1"}],"/default-aid-type":[{"@code":"C01","@vocabulary":"1"}],"/default-tied-status@code":"5","/description":[{"/narrative":[{"1":"The overall objective of PROGRES is to improve the living conditions and food and nutrition security of the poor rural population (especially women and youth). Its development objective is to empower rural poor people, facilitating their sustainable access to natural resources and communal equipment. Ultimately, the objectives are: (i) 150,000 rural dwellers benefit from economic mobility; (ii) 50 per cent of the reclaimed land is regenerated; (iii) 60 per cent of the reclaimed land is improved; (iv) 30 per cent of households report an increase in production; (v) 90 per cent of communal infrastructure is operational.The overall objective of PROGRES is to improve the living conditions and food and nutrition security of the poor rural population (especially women and youth). Its development objective is to empower rural poor people, facilitating their sustainable access to natural resources and communal equipment. Ultimately, the objectives are: (i) 150,000 rural dwellers benefit from economic mobility; (ii) 50 per cent of the reclaimed land is regenerated; (iii) 60 per cent of the reclaimed land is improved; (iv) 30 per cent of households report an increase in production; (v) 90 per cent of communal infrastructure is operational.The overall objective of PROGRES is to improve the living conditions and food and nutrition security of the poor rural population (especially women